invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: a build declares a TLS cipher suite whose AEAD is AES-GCM and
  ct.h stops refusing it outside a host object and AES=extern, so the
  suite takes the device object's default, AES=soft. That build hands a
  traffic key to a cipher whose 256-byte S-box is indexed with the key:
  aes_expand_round_keys substitutes the key's own bytes before a block
  runs, sub_bytes substitutes counter ^ round_key once per round, and
  gcm_ghash inherits it because the hash subkey is aes_encrypt_block of a
  zero block. The fall back is silent -- every source compiles and every
  vector passes -- so the compiler's refusal is the only check, and this
  edit removes it.

--- old
#if !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN)
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM needs a host object or AES=extern: the AES=soft S-box reads the key"
#endif
--- new
